# Arc's File ▸ New Easel (⌃⇧E, Arc 1.172.1, docs/arc-parity.md "Easels, measured"): a Today tab on an
# easel:// address whose page is Niche's canvas, not a web page; it comes back after a relaunch.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
niche://action/newEasel
wait 2
niche://debug?browserWindows=created
expect-log Niche browser windows created: kind=normal .*tabs=\[easel://[0-9A-F-]{36}\] open=easel://[0-9A-F-]{36} page=1
relaunch
wait 4
niche://debug?browserWindows=relaunched
expect-log browser windows relaunched: kind=normal listed=1 tabs=1 open=1
niche://action/viewEasels
wait 1
# The capture menu's New Easel: an easel with the capture on it opens in a new tab (after the
# relaunch only niche.log is read, which counts tabs rather than naming them).
niche://open?url=${PAGE}?n=captured
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
niche://debug?captureToEasel=1
wait 2
niche://debug?browserWindows=captured
expect-log browser windows captured: kind=normal listed=1 tabs=3 open=1
# Send To… an easel: the capture lands on the easel edited last, next to the first one.
niche://open?url=${PAGE}?n=sent
wait 2
niche://debug?captureToEasel=send
expect-log capture sent to an easel, which now holds 2 items
